In the Health-RI Semantic Interoperability Initiative, we are building a shared semantic reference model to make meanings explicit and link standards (e.g., FHIR/OMOP/openEHR) via reusable mappings (instead of many pairwise mappings).

We just published a first version of our Sex & Gender ontology, and we’re inviting everyone to review it. Community participation is fundamental if this is to serve as shared semantics for linking standards: it builds trust, makes assumptions visible, and improves clarity and coverage.

What to review (any depth is welcome):
• domain correctness & coverage
• conceptual/modeling rigor (constructs, patterns, constraints)
• clarity (what’s unclear, missing, ambiguous, or misleading)

Join the review here: https://health-ri.github.io/semantic-interoperability/external-review/sex-and-gender

